# Reference session: reversed observation timestamps
# Demonstrates correct ticket field ordering when plate observations
# arrive in reverse chronological order.
# Three clients: C1 (camera), C2 (camera), D1 (dispatcher)

# Camera C1 identifies — 7 bytes
[00.000] C1 -> S: 80 00 32 00 0a 00 50

# Camera C2 identifies — 7 bytes
[00.010] C2 -> S: 80 00 32 00 1e 00 50

# Dispatcher D1 identifies — 4 bytes
[00.020] D1 -> S: 81 01 00 32

# C2 reports plate observation FIRST (chronologically later event) — 12 bytes
[00.100] C2 -> S: 20 06 46 41 53 54 39 39 00 00 c5 12

# C1 reports plate observation SECOND (chronologically earlier event) — 12 bytes
[00.200] C1 -> S: 20 06 46 41 53 54 39 39 00 00 c3 50

# Server sends ticket — note field ordering reflects chronological order,
# NOT arrival order. Earlier observation comes first in the ticket. — 24 bytes
[00.201] S -> D1: 21 06 46 41 53 54 39 39 00 32 00 0a 00 00 c3 50 00 1e 00 00 c5 12 3e 80
